{# Conventional Commits format template #}
{# description: Generates commit messages following Conventional Commits specification #}
{# variables: changes, repository, user #}

{%- macro get_change_type(changes) -%}
{%- if changes.is_feature %}feat{% elif changes.is_fix %}fix{% elif changes.is_refactor %}refactor{% elif changes.is_docs %}docs{% elif changes.is_test %}test{% else %}chore{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro format_diff_content(file) -%}
{%- if file.hunks %}
```diff
{%- for hunk in file.hunks[:3] %}
{%- if hunk.removed_lines %}
{%- for line in hunk.removed_lines[:8] %}
- {{ line[:120] }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if hunk.removed_lines|length > 8 %}
  ... ({{ hunk.removed_lines|length - 8 }} more removed lines)
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- if hunk.added_lines %}
{%- for line in hunk.added_lines[:8] %}
+ {{ line[:120] }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if hunk.added_lines|length > 8 %}
  ... ({{ hunk.added_lines|length - 8 }} more added lines)
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
```
{%- elif file.content_preview %}
```diff
{{ file.content_preview }}
```
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

Generate a commit message for the following changes:

## Summary
- Files changed: {{ changes.affected_files|length }}
- Lines added: +{{ changes.lines_added }}
- Lines removed: -{{ changes.lines_deleted }}
- Suggested type: {{ get_change_type(changes) }}
{%- if changes.scope %}
- Scope: {{ changes.scope }}
{%- endif %}

## Changed Files
{% for file in changes.affected_files %}
### {{ file.path }} ({{ file.change_type }}, +{{ file.lines_added }}/-{{ file.lines_deleted }})
{%- if file.is_test %} [TEST]{% endif %}
{%- if file.is_config %} [CONFIG]{% endif %}
{%- if file.is_docs %} [DOCS]{% endif %}

{{ format_diff_content(file) }}
{% endfor %}

## Instructions
Based on the code diff above, generate a commit message that:
1. Has a clear, specific subject line in format: type(scope): description
2. Describes WHAT the code changes actually do (not generic phrases like "update code")
3. Uses imperative mood ("add", "fix", "refactor", not "added", "fixed")
4. Is specific about the actual change (e.g., "add retry logic for API timeouts" not "improve API")

Output ONLY the commit message, nothing else. Format:

type(scope): subject line here

Optional body paragraph explaining why if the change is complex.
